{"id":"8dc769bd-fd46-4a75-b986-6277d8a5f991","object":"chat.completion","created":1785006004,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        for key in [\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"]:\\n            if key not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call missing {key}\\\")\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be boolean\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        accept = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accept,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 10)\\n        })\\n        if accept:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` according to the given task. The task is AGENT-TF-01: \"API-call filtering with supplied token losses\". The input `case` is a payload object containing `threshold` and `calls` (list of call objects). Each call has `call_id`, `loss_without_call`, `loss_with_call`, `prediction_tokens`, `parseable`. We need to compute per-call gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalize gain by dividing by prediction_tokens (number of prediction tokens). Then check if `parseable` is true and normalized_gain >= threshold. If both satisfied, the call is accepted. We need to return `accepted_call_ids` (list of call_id strings) and `diagnostics` (list of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain). Diagnostics must be in the same order as the input calls. Normalized_gain should be rounded? The candidate_artifact says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" The output schema requires normalized_gain as number. So we need to round? The candidate says \"rounded\". Probably round to some default? Possibly to e.g., 10 decimal places? But the schema does not specify precision. In the public fixtures, the losses are given with high precision. We should preserve as computed, but maybe round to avoid floating-point artifacts? The instruction says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". I think rounding is expected but not specified. Common rounding would be to maybe 6 decimal places? However, the candidate artifact doesn't specify. We can round to a reasonable number, e.g., 10 decimal places, or just return the float as computed. But to be safe, I'll round to 10 decimal places, or use `round(normalized_gain, 10)`. The output must be JSON-serializable. We'll use Python's `float`.\n\nImplementation steps:\n- Validate input: expect `threshold` (number) and `calls` (list). Each call must have required fields. If missing, raise ValueError.\n- For each call:\n  - Compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call\n  - normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (if prediction_tokens > 0; but assume positive as per definition)\n  - accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n  - Append diagnostic object: {\"call_id\": call_id, \"accepted\": accepted, \"normalized_gain\": rounded_value}\n- Collect accepted_call_ids: for each accepted call, add its call_id.\n- Return dict with \"accepted_call_ids\" and \"diagnostics\".\n\nWe must not mutate input. Use standard library only.\n\nWe need to wrap the function in JSON with key \"implementation\". The response must be a single JSON object with that key.\n\nLet's write the Python code:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate required fields\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing calls\")\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be a number\")\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        # Validate call\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"each call must be a dict\")\n        for key in [\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"]:\n            if key not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"call missing {key}\")\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_without_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_with_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be boolean\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        accept = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accept,\n            \"normalized_gain\": round(normalized_gain, 10)\n        })\n        if accept:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWe need to ensure that the rounding is appropriate. The candidate says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". We'll round to 10 decimal places. If the threshold is 0.05, rounding to 10 should be fine.\n\nWe must output as JSON string with the \"implementation\" key.\n\nThus final response:\n{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        for key in [\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"]:\\n            if key not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call missing {key}\\\")\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(tokens, int) or tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be boolean\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        accept = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accept,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": round(normalized_gain, 10)\\n        })\\n        if accept:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"}\n\nMake sure to escape quotes and newlines properly. Also ensure no trailing whitespace. We'll output exactly as required."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2171,"completion_tokens":2272,"total_tokens":4443,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1708},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":123},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}